{"type":"assistant","uuid":"32e0e4ce-1eab-4f13-bf23-87c1fd0a2bfe","session_id":"6e908e0e-2ee7-431d-b303-30aaa260a97f","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"32e0e4ce-1eab-4f13-bf23-87c1fd0a2bfe","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nFix confirmed on disk. The patch file is at `fix.patch`. Here's the final output:\n\n---\n\n## Root Cause\n\nIn **`TotpProgressBar.java`** at the `refresh()` method, the animation calculates `animPart = maxProgress / _period`. With `maxProgress = 100` (default ProgressBar max) and `_period = 9999`:\n\n```\nanimPart = 100 / 9999 = 0   ← integer division rounds to zero\nanimEnd = currentProgress / 0 * 0  ← ArithmeticException: divide by zero → CRASH\n```\n\nThe value `9999` passes all validation in `TotpInfo.isPeriodValid()` (which only checks `period > 0` and `period <= 2147483`), but the progress bar has a much smaller practical limit.\n\n## Fix\n\nClamp `_period` to `maxProgress` before the division:\n\n```diff\n+        int effectivePeriod = Math.min(_period, maxProgress);\n-        int animPart = maxProgress / _period;\n+        int animPart = maxProgress / effectivePeriod;\n```\n\nWith the fix: `effectivePeriod = min(9999, 100) = 100`, so `animPart = 100 / 100 = 1` — no divide-by-zero.\n\n## Patch\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/app/src/main/java/com/beemdevelopment/aegis/ui/views/TotpProgressBar.java b/app/src/main/java/com/beemdevelopment/aegis/ui/views/TotpProgressBar.java\n--- a/app/src/main/java/com/beemdevelopment/aegis/ui/views/TotpProgressBar.java\n+++ b/app/src/main/java/com/beemdevelopment/aegis/ui/views/TotpProgressBar.java\n@@ -63,9 +63,13 @@ public class TotpProgressBar extends ProgressBar {\n         long millisTillRotation = TotpInfo.getMillisTillNextRotation(_period);\n         int currentProgress = (int) (maxProgress * ((float) millisTillRotation / (_period * 1000)));\n \n+        // clamp period to maxProgress to avoid integer division resulting in zero\n+        // which would cause division-by-zero in the animation calculations below\n+        int effectivePeriod = Math.min(_period, maxProgress);\n+\n         // start progress animation, compensating for any changes to the animator duration scale settings\n-        int animPart = maxProgress / _period;\n+        int animPart = maxProgress / effectivePeriod;\n         int animEnd = (currentProgress / animPart) * animPart;\n         int animPartDuration = (int) (1000 / _animDurationScale);\n         float animDurationFraction = (float) (currentProgress - animEnd) / animPart;\n```\n\n**Note:** The build cannot complete from this environment due to network restrictions (jcenter.bintray.com is offline), but the change is a single variable substitution with correct Java syntax — no imports or type changes needed."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50826,"output_tokens":684,"cache_read_input_tokens":50304,"total_tokens":51510}}}
