below\n+        int effectivePeriod = Math.min(_period, maxProgress);\n+\n         // start progress animation, compensating for any changes to the animator duration scale settings\n-        int animPart = maxProgress / _period;\n+        int animPart = maxProgress / effectivePeriod;\n         int animEnd = (currentProgress / animPart) * animPart;\n         int animPartDuration = (int) (1000 / _animDurationScale);\n         float animDurationFraction = (float) (currentProgress - animEnd) / animPart;\n```\n\n**Note:** The build cannot complete from this environment due to network restrictions (jcenter.bintray.com is offline), but the change is a single variable substitution with correct Java syntax — no imports or type changes needed.","usage":{"input_tokens":1465564,"output_tokens":17221,"cache_read_input_tokens":1259696,"total_tokens":1482785},"permission_denials":[]}
